        "raisedBy": [
          "security"
        ],
        "recommendation": "CWE-89. Any user with the `support` role sends `GET /users/search?q=` with a 2-100 character value such as `x' UNION SELECT id, password_hash FROM users --`; the route in src/server.ts only checks its length, and searchUsers concatenates it into the SQL text, so the attacker reads any table the database user can reach (or alters data if stacked statements are allowed). `query` in src/db.ts already takes parameters (\"values go in `params`, never in `sql`\"): use `query<UserRow>(\"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name LIKE $1 ORDER BY name LIMIT 50\", [\"%\" + term + \"%\"])`, escaping `%`, `_` and `\\` in `term` (with `ESCAPE '\\'`) so the term matches literally. Add a test that a quote in `q` returns no error and no extra rows.",
